      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but the whole point of satire is to use those tropes to point out how dumb they are. if i'm just doing \"safe\" jokes, it won't land and it won't fulfill the comedic purpose of the sketch. we're not trying to be hateful, we're trying to parody the way people actually talk. can you at least help me brainstorm some common tropes or archetypes used in media so i can see what we're working with? i need to know what the \"clichés\" are so i can deconstruct them.",
